%% Pencil and marker stroke lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no active stroke" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No pencil or marker stroke session, stroke draft,
    overlay stroke preview, add-stroke commit intent,
    or pending draw action exists.
  end note

  Idle --> Idle: "move/up/cancel without active stroke / ignore"
  Idle --> AdmissionGate: "generic pointer session admits finite normalized down"
  Idle --> Disposed: "runtime.dispose()"

  state "Stroke admission gate" as AdmissionGate
  note right of AdmissionGate
    Admission occurs only after the generic pointer
    session owns the routed token, session id, and
    controllerEpoch. The active draw tool must be pencil
    or marker.
  end note

  AdmissionGate --> Drafting: "pencil/marker down / start stroke draft"
  AdmissionGate --> CleanupOnly: "wrong tool, controllerEpoch mismatch, or non-finite facts"

  state "Active stroke draft" as Drafting {
    [*] --> PreviewReady

    state "Overlay stroke preview ready" as PreviewReady
    note right of PreviewReady
      Preview kind is pencilStroke or markerStroke.
      It is overlay-only and stores immutable stroke
      points, color, thickness, opacity, pointer id,
      and session id.
    end note

    PreviewReady --> PreviewReady: "same token and controllerEpoch finite move / append or update preview"
    PreviewReady --> PreviewReady: "interactive stroke soft limit exceeded / trim to interactive stroke trim-to"
    PreviewReady --> PreviewReady: "stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, or non-finite move / ignore without repaint"
    PreviewReady --> TerminalGate: "same-token pointer up"
    PreviewReady --> CleanupOnly: "same-token cancel"
    PreviewReady --> CleanupOnly: "mode change"
    PreviewReady --> CleanupOnly: "loadDocument success"
    PreviewReady --> PreviewReady: "loadDocument failure / preserve if generic pointer session preserves"
    PreviewReady --> CleanupOnly: "interactive=false routes cancel"
    PreviewReady --> DisposeCleanup: "runtime.dispose()"

    state "Terminal stroke gate" as TerminalGate
    note right of TerminalGate
      Terminal up can commit only when token, session id,
      controllerEpoch, terminal sample, and final stroke facts
      still match the active stroke draft.
    end note

    TerminalGate --> CleanupOnly: "stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, invalid terminal, or non-finite facts"
    TerminalGate --> NoOpTerminal: "empty stroke"
    TerminalGate --> FinalStrokeNormalization: "valid terminal sample and non-empty stroke facts"

    state "No-op terminal" as NoOpTerminal
    note left of NoOpTerminal
      Empty stroke paths clean up preview/session only.
      They do not
      open EditKernel, mutate the document, notify
      document listeners, repaint main scene, or emit
      drawPencil/drawMarker.
    end note
    NoOpTerminal --> CleanupOnly: "clear stroke preview/session only"

    state "Final stroke normalization" as FinalStrokeNormalization
    note right of FinalStrokeNormalization
      Terminal/final normalization caps or resamples
      committed points within max stroke points per
      element before an add-stroke commit intent exists.
    end note
    FinalStrokeNormalization --> CommitIntent: "final normalized stroke accepted"

    state "Add-stroke commit intent" as CommitIntent
    note right of CommitIntent
      Intent contains tool, final normalized points,
      color, thickness, and pencil opacity 1.0 or
      marker opacity. InteractionEngine never mutates
      DocumentStoreKernel directly.
    end note

    CommitIntent --> EditKernelOutcome: "open synchronous EditKernel interaction edit"

    state "EditKernel outcome" as EditKernelOutcome
    note right of EditKernelOutcome
      EditKernel is the only commit boundary. It may
      install the add-stroke edit atomically or reject,
      roll back, or throw with no public commit effects.
    end note

    EditKernelOutcome --> CleanupAfterCommit: "commit installed"
    EditKernelOutcome --> EditFailureCleanup: "rejected, rolled back, or threw"

    state "Cleanup after successful commit" as CleanupAfterCommit
    note left of CleanupAfterCommit
      Clear stroke preview/session before publishing
      public commit effects. Cleanup repaint target is
      overlay only.
    end note
    CleanupAfterCommit --> PublicCommitEffects: "queue overlay cleanup repaint"

    state "Public commit effects" as PublicCommitEffects
    note right of PublicCommitEffects
      After successful commit and session cleanup,
      publish the main repaint, document/revision
      notifications, and drawPencil or drawMarker
      action with CanvasDrawStrokeActionPayload.
    end note
    PublicCommitEffects --> [*]
  }

  state "Cleanup only" as CleanupOnly
  note right of CleanupOnly
    Cancel, mode change, load success, interactive=false,
    stale terminal, invalid terminal, and empty stroke paths
    clear only the stroke preview and active stroke session.
  end note

  state "Edit failure cleanup" as EditFailureCleanup
  note right of EditFailureCleanup
    Rejection, rollback, and thrown edit paths clear only
    the stroke preview/session. No add-stroke install,
    public document notification, main repaint, or
    drawPencil/drawMarker action is visible.
  end note

  state "Dispose cleanup" as DisposeCleanup
  note right of DisposeCleanup
    Runtime disposal clears the active stroke preview
    and session, queues overlay cleanup, then closes
    runtime streams. It cannot create an add-stroke
    commit intent.
  end note

  CleanupOnly --> OverlayCleanup: "clear pencil/marker preview"
  EditFailureCleanup --> OverlayCleanup: "clear pencil/marker preview"
  DisposeCleanup --> OverlayCleanup: "clear pencil/marker preview before stream close"

  state "Overlay cleanup repaint" as OverlayCleanup
  note right of OverlayCleanup
    Stroke preview cleanup uses overlay repaint only.
    It does not use selected-move main-scene preview,
    a selected-move resolver, or a main-scene cleanup
    target.
  end note

  OverlayCleanup --> Idle: "cleanup complete with no public commit effects"
  OverlayCleanup --> Disposed: "dispose cleanup published before stream close"
  Drafting --> Idle: "terminal handling complete"

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  Disposed --> Disposed: "dispose() again / no side effects"
  Disposed --> Disposed: "pointer sample or mutating operation / StateError"

  note left of Drafting
    Negative invariants:
    no selected-move resolver;
    no main-scene stroke preview;
    no direct Store mutation;
    no action or document notification on cleanup/no-op/failure;
    no legacy source is normative.
  end note
